          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Later Years and Struggles</strong><br>\nIn his later years, Kurosawa faced several challenges, including a suicide attempt and difficulties securing funding for his films. However, he persevered and continued to create influential films like \"Kagemusha\" (1980) and \"Ran\" (1985).</p>\n\n<p><strong>Legacy and Influence</strong><br>\nKurosawa's influence on filmmaking is vast, with his techniques and storytelling inspiring directors across the world. His legacy is cemented by his contribution to the development of the modern film epic and his timeless storytelling.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Recognition and Awards</strong><br>\nKurosawa was awarded the Academy Honorary Award in 1990 for his lifetime of cinematic achievements. He is remembered not only as a cornerstone of Japanese cinema but also as a figure who shaped the medium internationally until his death on September 6, 1998.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
